    "narrative": "Today\u2019s outlook for the Austin Waves centers on the high-upside matchup for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries the day\u2019s premier efficiency score at 70.14. Facing Legumina, whose 4.32 xERA suggests a prime opportunity for extra-base production, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable park factor (+3%) and a strong lineup position batting second. While **Drake Baldwin** is currently our only other start pushing near the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold, his 59.85 rating against Hart is bolstered by a leadoff spot that provides premium plate appearance volume. Despite Hart\u2019s moderate 3.98 xERA, **Drake Baldwin**\u2019s role as the table-setter provides the floor necessary to maintain our rate categories.\n\nThe rest of the active roster presents a more conservative profile. **Brayan Rocchio** (46.89) faces a stiff challenge against Bradley, T; while his spot in the four-hole adds marginal value, his score is hampered by the opposing arm\u2019s skill set. **Dominic Smith** (40.47) remains our most vulnerable start, narrowly clearing the 40-point bench floor. His L/L matchup against Hart is sub-optimal, and his position at the bottom of the order (-3%) confirms his status as a fill-in rather than a core contributor. With stars like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** all sidelined by team off-days, we are forced to lean on the depth of **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Jordan Westburg**\u2014none of whom were available to boost our efficiency today. We will continue to monitor the status of **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, and **Coby Mayo** for future series, but for today, the Waves must play for efficiency over ceiling.",
